module

public import Sheaf.RingTheory.GlobalDimension
public import Sheaf.RingTheory.Depth
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.LocalRing.ResidueField.Basic
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Noetherian.Defs
import Sheaf.RingTheory.MinimalFiniteFreeResolutionLocal
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.ExactFreeComplexLastMinors

@[expose] public section

universe u

namespace Ring

/-- Finite projective dimension of the residue field is bounded by local depth.
Source: Stacks Project, Algebra, proof of Lemma Tag 00OB, through the assertion
that the last-minor ideal has depth at least the last nonzero resolution degree.
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-residue-field-pd-le-depth)

Proof: Put d = pd_R kappa. Its defining minimum supplies a projective resolution
of length at most d. The residue field is finite, generated by the class of 1.
Apply exists_minimal_finite_free_resolution to obtain a finite free resolution
whose positive differentials have image in the maximal ideal times their targets.
Choose bases and let n be its largest nonzero degree; this exists since the
augmentation surjects onto the nonzero residue field. Truncating above n leaves
an exact projective resolution, so d <= n by minimality. For n = 0 the result
follows from nonnegativity of depth. For n >= 1, in the chosen bases the image
condition puts every differential coefficient in the maximal ideal. Apply
exact_free_complex_last_minors_regular_sequence to the truncated complex.
The last free rank is positive, so each maximal minor is a sum of products of
at least one coefficient in the maximal ideal. Thus the last-minor ideal is
contained in that proper ideal and cannot be the whole ring. The other branch
of the minors theorem supplies an R-regular sequence of length n there, hence
in the maximal ideal. The definition of depth as the supremum of lengths of
such sequences gives n <= depth R (also if depth is infinite). Combining
these inequalities proves d <= depth R. -/
theorem residueField_projectiveDimension_le_depth
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    (h : ModuleCat.HasFiniteProjectiveDimension
      (ModuleCat.of R (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R))) :
    (ModuleCat.projectiveDimension
      (ModuleCat.of R (IsLocalRing.ResidueField R)) h : ℕ∞) ≤
        IsLocalRing.depth (R := R) R := by
  sorry

end Ring
